body: "## Reproduced boundary\n\nLow-priority path-fidelity edge case on main `eac19c5bf3ceb7a82f1e958ac97bef4d9af16fc6`, Node v24.19.0/Linux and the exact committed SDK `2026.10.13` dependency graph.\n\nA valid Git repository whose directory name ends with a space cannot use `--changed`. The new [file-focus root discovery](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/blob/eac19c5bf3ceb7a82f1e958ac97bef4d9af16fc6/file-focus.ts#L65-L86) calls `.trim()` on `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`, deleting the actual final character of the directory name. Subsequent Git commands run against a different/nonexistent path and the error incorrectly recommends fetching a known base.\n\nThe [documented goal](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/blob/eac19c5bf3ceb7a82f1e958ac97bef4d9af16fc6/README.md#L56-L86) is file focus from a real Git working repository with actionable errors for invalid repositories/bases. Here the repository and its main commit are both valid.\n\n## Small real-Git reproduction\n\nRun from the reviewed package after installing its locked dependencies:\n\n```js\nimport { mkdtempSync, mkdirSync, writeFileSync, renameSync, rmSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport { tmpdir } from \"node:os\";\nimport { join } from \"node:path\";\nimport { execFileSync } from \"node:child_process\";\nimport { resolveFileFocus } from \"./dist/file-focus.js\";\n\nconst parent = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), \"focus-space-\"));\nconst root = join(parent, \"project \");\nmkdirSync(root);\nconst git = (...args) => execFileSync(\"git\", [\n  \"-c\", \"user.name=Fixture\", \"-c\", \"user.email=<fixture address>\", ...args,\n], { cwd: root, encoding: \"utf8\" });\n\ntry {\n  git(\"init\", \"-b\", \"main\");\n  writeFileSync(join(root, \"file.ts\"), \"initial\");\n  git(\"add\", \".\");\n  git(\"commit\", \"-m\", \"Base\");\n  writeFileSync(join(root, \"file.ts\"), \"changed\");\n\n  console.log(JSON.stringify(git(\"rev-parse\", \"--show-toplevel\")));\n  try {\n    console.log(resolveFileFocus({ changed: true }, [], root, join(root, \".agents/pm\")));\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.log(error.code, error.exitCode);\n  }\n\n  const normal = join(parent, \"project\");\n  renameSync(root, normal);\n  console.log(resolveFileFocus({ changed: true }, [], normal, join(normal, \".agents/pm\")));\n} finally {\n  rmSync(parent, { recursive: true, force: true });\n}\n```\n\nActual:\n- Git reports the correct root, ending in `\"project \\\\n\"`\n- Space-suffixed root: `UNKNOWN_BASE`, exit code 2\n- Rename the same repository to `project`, without changing its contents/history: succeeds with `files: [\"file.ts\"]`\n\nThe direct helper failure proves pm-context itself loses the path even when given the correct cwd. A second end-to-end control used a real SDK-initialized tracker with the built extension: ordinary `context-pack --format json` succeeded in the space-suffixed directory, but `context-pack --changed main --format json` exited 2 with “File focus requires a Git working repository.” That host path can already be normalized before reaching the helper, so fixing this helper alone should not be assumed to close the installed-CLI case.\n\n## Expected and scope\n\nPreserve the exact repository root returned by Git, removing only Git's terminating newline rather than meaningful filename whitespace. The same working repository should select the same changed file before and after the directory rename.\n\nThis is a narrow Unix path edge case, not a general failure of normal paths or spaces inside names. No tracker corruption or data loss was observed. The 17 authored file-focus tests pass on ordinary roots.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Real Git regression with a trailing-space repository directory\n- Same-repository rename control with unchanged history and contents\n- Public helper and installed-CLI paths both work, or clearly separate any required host-side correction\n- Continue rejecting truly missing repositories and unknown bases\n\n## Duplicate check\n\nReviewed all 152 pre-existing GitHub issues/PRs across all states plus current canonical PM issues/features; no matching path-fidelity defect report was present. The related feature owner is [pm-context-ax7z](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/blob/eac19c5bf3ceb7a82f1e958ac97bef4d9af16fc6/.agents/pm/features/pm-context-ax7z.toon), delivered through [PR #151](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/pull/151). Issue #153 is the separately reproduced overlap-packing defect. No implementation changes or dependency-pin changes were made.\n\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (1)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-24T07:53:20Z)\n>\n> Additional bounded verification on main `b8a0d864335003ed67ae6a79478c30c30870d1de`, Node 24.22.1/Linux, Git 2.52.0: the installed-CLI portion still has an ancestor-repository edge case after #166. This is not attributed to #170, which does not change the file-focus implementation.\n> \n> The exact source files were verified against Git blob SHAs; TypeScript 7.0.2 builds byte-identical committed dist. The checked-in regression command:\n> \n> `node --test --test-name-pattern=\"trailing-whitespace roots work\" test/file-focus.test.ts`\n> \n> fails with the pinned official PM CLI 2026.10.23. A separate executable-only comparison with official 2026.10.24 fails too. Basic context-pack succeeds, but `context-pack --changed main --format json` exits 2 rather than selecting the linked changed file. Direct helper whitespace tests and ordinary-path controls pass.\n> \n> To isolate shared-environment ancestry, I made only this fixture change in a separate test copy: immediately after the fixture creates its temporary parent, run its existing `git(parent, \"init\", \"-b\", \"outer\")` helper. This creates an explicit, valid outer Git repository containing the already-existing inner `project ` repository. The whitespace-root CLI test then fails with “Cannot resolve the Git base or a common ancestor with HEAD.” Running the same nested fixture with an ordinary `project` directory passes. Both fixtures contain their own inner main branch and identical changed-file setup.\n> \n> A diagnostic-only installed-copy run (not the pass/fail oracle) showed the process cwd retaining the correct trailing-space root while the host repository context selected an ancestor. The recovery guard in [file-focus.ts](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/blob/b8a0d864335003ed67ae6a79478c30c30870d1de/file-focus.ts#L73-L78) accepts the actual working root only when its trimmed spelling equals the supplied host cwd; the observed ancestor context does not satisfy that condition. This narrows the remaining boundary, not a complete host root-cause determination.\n> \n> Impact remains narrow: Unix trailing-whitespace repository directories, with ancestor-repository context. No tracker loss/corruption was observed. Do not infer ordinary paths fail. Original isolated files and project pins were not edited; auxiliary copied pm-ops/changelog dependencies were 2026.10.19 rather than the project's 10.20 pins, so this is not whole-release certification.\n> \n> Acceptance follow-through: retain the passing direct-helper and ordinary-path controls, and make the installed-CLI test pass when a trailing-space inner Git repository has an explicit outer Git repository. Preserve exact cwd identity without accidentally selecting the ancestor or weakening non-Git/base validation. See the existing [file-focus contract and whitespace-root documentation](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/blob/b8a0d864335003ed67ae6a79478c30c30870d1de/README.md).\n> \n> All-status issue/PR inventory and this thread were checked again before adding evidence; no duplicate issue is being opened."
